{"abstract":"Understanding software systems is a vital task, often undertaken by teams of engineers, for the development and maintenance of systems. Collaborative software visualization tools are essential in this context, yet they are limited. Existing tools, particularly in virtual reality, allow exploration but lack the crucial feature of note-taking, which is a significant limitation. We introduce Immersive Software Archaeology (ISA), a virtual reality tool that enables engineering teams to collaboratively explore and comprehend software systems. Unique to ISA, it facilitates note-taking during exploration with virtual multimedia whiteboards that support freehand diagramming, audio recordings, and VR screenshots. Notes taken on these whiteboards are synchronized with an Integrated Development Environment (IDE), providing easy access to the results of a VR exploration while performing changes to the system’s source code.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hoff, Adrian","Lungu, Mircea","Seidl, Christoph","Lanza, Michele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730169"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Università della Svizzera italiana"],"keyword":["Collaborative Software Engineering","Software Comprehension","Software Visualization","Virtual reality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immersive software archaeology collaborative exploration and note taking in virtual reality","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103694536/2024-icpc_-_isa_-_collaborative_exploration_note_taking_virtual_reality_tool_-_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-730169","identifier":[{"id":"85197284794","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-550e656b-4243-4bc9-8967-a34285c02d1a"],"keyword":["Collaborative Software Engineering","Software Comprehension","Software Visualization","Virtual Reality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B3914CFD61760353E21C4B4BA297FF1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103694536/2024-icpc_-_isa_-_collaborative_exploration_note_taking_virtual_reality_tool_-_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"università della svizzera italiana","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Università della Svizzera italiana","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Adrian","key":"hoffpau","last":"Hoff","locid":"6a57a243-af32-4e1d-849c-75146da60102","name":"Hoff, Adrian","orcid":"0000-0002-5254-6246","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph","key":"seidlpau","last":"Seidl","locid":"fda8c630-1b0a-4910-ae2a-602850616275","name":"Seidl, Christoph","orcid":"0000-0003-4539-8297","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"lanzapau","last":"Lanza","name":"Lanza, Michele","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643916.3644438","pages":"387-391","status":"p","title":"32nd IEEE/ACM International Conference on Program Comprehension (ICPC ’24)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197284794"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-550e656b-4243-4bc9-8967-a34285c02d1a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Immersive Software Archaeology: Collaborative Exploration and Note Taking in Virtual Reality","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730169","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Exploring and comprehending a software system, e.g., as preparation for its re-engineering, is a relevant, yet challenging endeavour often conducted by teams of engineers. Collaborative exploration tools aim to ease the process, e.g., via interactive visualizations in virtual reality (VR). However, these neglect to provide engineers with capabilities for persisting their thoughts and findings. We present an interactive VR visualization method that enables (distributed) teams of engineers to collaboratively (1) explore a subject system, while (2) persisting insights via free-hand diagrams, audio recordings, and in-visualization VR screenshots. We invited pairs of software engineering practitioners to use our method to collaboratively explore a software system. We observed how they used our method and collected their feedback and impressions before replaying their findings to the original developers of the subject system for assessment.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hoff, Adrian","Lungu, Mircea","Seidl, Christoph","Lanza, Michele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730177"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Università della Svizzera italiana"],"keyword":["Collaborative Software Engineering","Software Comprehension","Software Visualization","Virtual reality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collaborative software exploration with multimedia note taking in virtual reality","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103694435/2024-icpc_-_collaborative_exploration_multimedia_note_taking_virtual_reality_-_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Hoff and Seidl are supported by the DFF (Independent Research Fund Denmark) project “Immersive Software Archaeology (ISA)” (0136-00070B). Lanza is supported by the Swiss National Science Foundation (SNSF) project “INSTINCT” (Project No. 190113)."],"id":"S01-000.00-730177","identifier":[{"id":"85197281862","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-811cf3d3-78b1-4b95-9d62-bb9fe1d09121"],"keyword":["Collaborative Software Engineering","Software Comprehension","Software Visualization","Virtual Reality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B904066585D7F2F5A83D64FEB350BA66"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103694435/2024-icpc_-_collaborative_exploration_multimedia_note_taking_virtual_reality_-_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"università della svizzera italiana","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Università della Svizzera italiana","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Adrian","key":"hoffpau","last":"Hoff","locid":"6a57a243-af32-4e1d-849c-75146da60102","name":"Hoff, Adrian","orcid":"0000-0002-5254-6246","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph","key":"seidlpau","last":"Seidl","locid":"fda8c630-1b0a-4910-ae2a-602850616275","name":"Seidl, Christoph","orcid":"0000-0003-4539-8297","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"lanzapau","last":"Lanza","name":"Lanza, Michele","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643916.3644427","pages":"346-357","status":"p","title":"32nd IEEE/ACM International Conference on Program Comprehension (ICPC ’24)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197281862"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-811cf3d3-78b1-4b95-9d62-bb9fe1d09121"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Collaborative Software Exploration with Multimedia Note Taking in Virtual Reality","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730177","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we present the course “DevOps, Software Evolution, and Software Maintenance” that we developed and teach at IT University of Copenhagen. It differs from similar courses in that it focuses student project work on maintenance and evolution of a live software system.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pfeiffer, Helge","Lungu, Mircea","Tell, Paolo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712505"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer Science Education","Education","Educational courses","Maintenance engineering","Monitoring","Production","Software Engineering","Training"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"live is life teaching software engineering on live systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/MS.2023.3311376","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712505","identifier":[{"id":"85171528508","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2ae02a19-1699-4e52-8179-3d7f53e300f7"],"keyword":["Computer science education","Education","Educational courses","Maintenance engineering","Monitoring","Production","Software engineering","Training"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD054F4A3EE6E788EA4524747CDCD46F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102402128/SWSI-2023-02-0022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/MS.2023.3311376","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Danish Institute for IT Program Management","IT University of Copenhagen, Research Centre for Government IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ms.2023.3311376","issn":["07407459"],"issue":"6","journal":"IEEE Software","pages":"117-125","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Software","title_org":"I E E E Software","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171528508"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2ae02a19-1699-4e52-8179-3d7f53e300f7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Live Is Life: Teaching Software Engineering on Live Systems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712505","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Re-architecting a software system requires significant preparation, e.g., to scope and design new modules with their boundaries and constituent classes. When planning an intended future state of a system as a re-engineering goal, engineers often fall recur to mechanisms such as freehand sketching (using a whiteboard). While this ensures flexibility and expressiveness, the sketches remain disconnected from the source code. The alternative, tool-supported diagramming on the other hand considerably restricts flexibility and impedes free-form communication. We present a method for preparing the architectural software re-engineering via freehand sketches in virtual reality (VR) that can be seamlessly integrated with the model structure of a software visualization and, thus, also the code of a system, for productive use: Engineers explore a subject system in the immersive visualization, while freehand sketching their insights and plans. Our concept automatically interprets sketched shapes and connects them to the system’s source code, and superimposes code-level references into a sketch to support engineers in reflecting on their sketches. We evaluated our method in an iterative interview-based case study with software developers from four different companies, where they planned a hypothetical re-engineering of an opensource software system. Video Demonstration — https://youtu.be/NKC5YpH3n4Y","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hoff, Adrian","Seidl, Christoph","Lungu, Mircea","Lanza, Michele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712540"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Università della Svizzera italiana"],"keyword":["Reflexion Models","Software Re Engineering","Software Visualization","Virtual reality","Whiteboard Sketching"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preparing software re engineering via freehand sketches in virtual reality","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102214462/model-based-vr-whiteboard-preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Hoff and Seidl are supported by the DFF (Independent Research Fund Denmark) within the project “Immersive Software Archaeology (ISA)” (0136-00070B). Lanza is supported by the Swiss National Science Foundation (SNSF) through the project “INSTINCT” (Project No. 190113)."],"id":"S01-000.00-712540","identifier":[{"id":"85181533358","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-95253343-495f-41fe-baea-2c1c0140bde5"],"keyword":["Reflexion Models","Software Re-Engineering","Software Visualization","Virtual Reality","Whiteboard Sketching"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-69AE229AE5CB8FFD87D92A40B473844C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102214462/model-based-vr-whiteboard-preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"università della svizzera italiana","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Università della Svizzera italiana","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Adrian","key":"hoffpau","last":"Hoff","locid":"6a57a243-af32-4e1d-849c-75146da60102","name":"Hoff, Adrian","orcid":"0000-0002-5254-6246","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph","key":"seidlpau","last":"Seidl","locid":"fda8c630-1b0a-4910-ae2a-602850616275","name":"Seidl, Christoph","orcid":"0000-0003-4539-8297","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"lanzapau","last":"Lanza","name":"Lanza, Michele","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","subtitle":"ICSME 2023","title":"39th IEEE International Conference on Software Maintenance and Evolution"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-95253343-495f-41fe-baea-2c1c0140bde5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Preparing Software Re-Engineering via Freehand Sketches in Virtual Reality","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712540","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This paper explores redirection of activity as an intervention strategy for self-regulation online. We conducted an explorative study (N = 19) of the browser extension Aiki, which redirects a user from a self-defined ‘time-wasting’ website to an online platform for learning programming (Sololearn, Codecademy, or Udemy). Based on quantitative measures alone, using Aiki decreased the participants’ time spent on time-wasting websites on average, and increased programming knowledge. However, several users ended up avoiding their time-wasting websites entirely when Aiki was active, or they discontinued the use of the extension after ‘the novelty wore off’. Based on these effects, we qualitatively explored the user experiences and identified four challenges and four opportunities for using redirection of activity as an intervention strategy for self-regulation of time management in a browser. Our results suggest that this intervention strategy is promising, but careful design is necessary to strike an optimal balance between independence and regulation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Inie, Nanna","Westh, Bjørn Hjorth","Muller, John Henrik","Lungu, Mircea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718890"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Browser extension","Redirection of activity","Self regulation online","Time management","User experience analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"challenges and opportunities of using redirection of activity for self regulation online","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102539595/chi23-651-access.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718890","identifier":[{"id":"85160015709","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8dbec46b-156c-4d77-be71-b54b7ab6df38"],"keyword":["Browser extension","Redirection of activity","Self-regulation online","Time management","User experience analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD4EE2397687C55F0150E2C6F24DF203"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102539595/chi23-651-access.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjørn Hjorth","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","name":"Westh, Bjørn Hjorth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John Henrik","key":"mullerpau","last":"Muller","name":"Muller, John Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3544548.3581342","pages":"1-19","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"CHI '23: Proceedings of the 2023 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160015709"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8dbec46b-156c-4d77-be71-b54b7ab6df38"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Challenges and Opportunities of Using Redirection of Activity for Self-Regulation Online","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718890","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The assessment of repository evolution is particularly complex when one needs to analyze both 1) how the codebase is organized hierarchically and 2) how this codebase evolves over time. To address this problem, we developed GitTruck, a visualization tool that includes multiple views for the analysis of the evolution of hierarchically organized Git repositories. We conducted a preliminary user evaluation with 18 participants who, using a remote and asynchronous method, installed Git Truck, used it, and filled in a questionnaire to report their experience and impressions. We learned that participants consider particularly useful views that help them with understanding the contribution level of team members and views that highlight the parts of the system that change the most. The participants see Git Truck as a highly specialized tool; not for daily use but rather for a lower frequency of use.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lungu, Mircea","Højelse, Kristoffer","Kilbak, Thomas","Røssum, Jonas","Jäpelt, Emil","Merino, Leonel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383040"],"event":{"acronym":"VISSOFT","title":"IEEE Working Conference on Software Visualization"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","OECD"],"country":["Chile"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile"],"keyword":["Git analysis","Hierarchical code organization","Repository evolution","User evaluation","Visualization tool"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"git truck hierarchy oriented visualization of git repository evolution","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://mircealungu.com/docs/assets/papers/22-Git-Truck.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383040","identifier":[{"id":"85146248365","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-77fdb051-fd86-4fe1-82f0-3ffc0843289d"],"keyword":["Git analysis","Hierarchical code organization","Repository evolution","User evaluation","Visualization tool"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-628399FA5D4D4BFCB69CE44B06FB9955"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://mircealungu.com/docs/assets/papers/22-Git-Truck.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cl","key":"pontificia universidad católica de chile","loc":["Chile","America, South","OECD"],"name":"Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristoffer","key":"højelsepau","last":"Højelse","name":"Højelse, Kristoffer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"kilbakpau","last":"Kilbak","name":"Kilbak, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"røssumpau","last":"Røssum","name":"Røssum, Jonas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"jäpeltpau","last":"Jäpelt","name":"Jäpelt, Emil","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leonel","key":"merinopau","last":"Merino","name":"Merino, Leonel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/vissoft55257.2022.00021","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2022 Working Conference on Software Visualization (VISSOFT)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146248365"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-77fdb051-fd86-4fe1-82f0-3ffc0843289d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Git-Truck: Hierarchy-Oriented Visualization of Git Repository Evolution","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383040","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We propose to use reading time as a metric to report progress in language learning applications. As a case study we use a web-based application that enables learners of a foreign language to read texts from the web and practice vocabulary with interactive exercises generated based on their past readings. The application captures generic interactions with the web page (e.g. switching to a different tab) but also interactions directly related to language learning (e.g. clicking on a word to get a translation). We propose two metrics for approximating reading times based on user interactions with the web application. We analyze the correlation between these metrics and other interaction metrics and show that active time is the best metric for estimating the user’s actual involvement with the texts and that it can be approximated from interaction metrics","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lungu, Mircea","Hollenstein, Nora"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384920"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Second language learning","reading time","user interactions","web based learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analyzing user interactions to estimate reading time in web based l000000000002 reader applications","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14705/rpnet.2022.61.9782383720157","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384920","ids":["itu-f80cf0ec-0e4e-4cab-9631-fea7cee4ca33"],"keyword":["reading time","second language learning","user interactions","web-based learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8E02EA85E91B0BD2EFE6FC7ACBC95E3E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://research-publishing.net/publication/chapters/978-2-38372-015-7/1453.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14705/rpnet.2022.61.9782383720157","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nora","key":"hollensteinpau","last":"Hollenstein","name":"Hollenstein, Nora","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.14705/rpnet.2022.61.9782383720157","pages":"168-173","status":"p","title":"Intelligent CALL, granular systems and learner data: short papers from EUROCALL 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f80cf0ec-0e4e-4cab-9631-fea7cee4ca33"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Analyzing user interactions to estimate reading time in web-based L2 reader applications","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384920","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
