{"abstract":"In the past years numerous software visualization tools have been introduced to support the analysis of software systems and their evolution as captured in the versioning systems. Usually the target audience of such tools comprises software engineering professionals. In this paper we argue that such tools are also beneficial for educators who need to evaluate the quality of software systems developed by students. However, since the needs of educators are different than those of the software engineering professionals, we discuss several educator needs first. We report several usage examples that we believe are useful for educators when using repository visualization tools. We illustrate them with examples from several student projects from different courses in two universities. We conclude with a series of considerations that should be heeded by both educators and future tool-builders.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lungu, Mircea","Pfeiffer, Helge","D'Ambros, Marco","Lanza, Michele","Findhal, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382077"],"event":{"acronym":"VISSOFT","title":"IEEE Working Conference on Software Visualization"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Università della Svizzera italiana"],"keyword":["Educational tools","Quality Evaluation","Repository Analysis","Software Engineering Education","Software Visualization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can git repository visualization support educators in assessing group projects","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://mircealungu.com/docs/assets/papers/22-Git-Vis-4Edu.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382077","identifier":[{"id":"85146244230","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-36e33b0b-30d1-4a9d-8c08-d74ad541aad6"],"keyword":["Educational Tools","Quality Evaluation","Repository Analysis","Software Engineering Education","Software Visualization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B5F55B221B1A0550AED9F6364C1BC11F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://mircealungu.com/docs/assets/papers/22-Git-Vis-4Edu.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"università della svizzera italiana","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Università della Svizzera italiana","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helge","key":"pfeifferpau","last":"Pfeiffer","locid":"51cfa226-5179-4a05-aa13-4a53f8de6404","name":"Pfeiffer, Helge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"dambrospau","last":"D'Ambros","name":"D'Ambros, Marco","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"lanzapau","last":"Lanza","name":"Lanza, Michele","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"findhalpau","last":"Findhal","name":"Findhal, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/vissoft55257.2022.00030","eisbn":["9781665480925"],"isbn":["9781665480932"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2022 Working Conference on Software Visualization (VISSOFT)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146244230"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-36e33b0b-30d1-4a9d-8c08-d74ad541aad6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Can Git Repository Visualization Support Educators in Assessing Group Projects?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382077","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Architectural views are expensive to maintain. Software systems continuously evolve, making architectural views outdated. We present Codoc, a continuous architectural documentation system. Codoc empowers users to utilize a code-driven architectural view specification language to create views that are continuously updated and accessible. Through qualitative studies, we find code driven view specification as a promising candidate to replace manual architectural visualization in software documentation.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Weiss Bang, Casper","Lungu, Mircea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382023"],"event":{"acronym":"VISSOFT","title":"IEEE Working Conference on Software Visualization"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Architectural Views","Continuous Documentation","Participatory Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"codoc code driven architectural view specification framework in python","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86386665/21_CoDoc_VISSOFT.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382023","identifier":[{"id":"85123382148","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-339163a4-eee2-4a16-bbb3-0ca7ae57e2dc"],"keyword":[", Continuous Documentation","Architectural Views","Participatory Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DAA50FBA12BA38B5076F1268D3F2A32F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86386665/21_CoDoc_VISSOFT.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper","key":"weissbangpau","last":"Weiss Bang","name":"Weiss Bang, Casper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/vissoft52517.2021.00023","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2021 Working Conference on Software Visualization (VISSOFT)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123382148"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-339163a4-eee2-4a16-bbb3-0ca7ae57e2dc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Codoc: Code-driven Architectural View Specification Framework in Python","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382023","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We report on the development of react-bratus, a prototype providing developers with an interactive web-based component hierarchy visualization for React-based projects. We continuously evaluate react-bratus in multiple iterations with junior developers and find that component hierarchy visualizations are a promising tool for helping novice developers reverse engineer React-based applications.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Boersma, Stephan","Lungu, Mircea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381852"],"event":{"acronym":"VISSOFT","title":"IEEE Working Conference on Software Visualization"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Software Visualization","component hierarchy","polymetric views","react js"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"react bratus visualising react component hierarchies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86386642/21_React_bratus_VISSOFT.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381852","identifier":[{"id":"85123353821","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-26646405-a418-442d-b342-168ce627a918"],"keyword":["component hierarchy","polymetric views","react.js","software visualization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-439270BFF63234B895D15F78A4D859A0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86386642/21_React_bratus_VISSOFT.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephan","key":"boersmapau","last":"Boersma","name":"Boersma, Stephan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/vissoft52517.2021.00025","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2021 Working Conference on Software Visualization (VISSOFT)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123353821"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-26646405-a418-442d-b342-168ce627a918"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"React-bratus: Visualising React Component Hierarchies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381852","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents and evaluates Aiki, a simple browser extension designed to redirect a user to a learning platform for a fixed amount of time before accessing websites defined as ’procrastination’ or ’time-wasting’ websites. The goal of the extension is to enable the user to exchange time spent on pages they believe contribute less to their own productivity for microlearning activities, defined as small or short-term learning activities. The paper describes the design and development of Aiki and evaluates the extension with a group of n = 10 participants studying the Danish language. Based on a two-week study, we conclude that this type of extension, even in its preliminary version, has the potential to improve language skills in a lightweight manner and that redirection is an important alternative to blocking for procrastination management.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Inie, Nanna","Lungu, Mircea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384034"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aiki","Browser extension","Educational technology","Language learning","Microlearning","Procrastination management","Productivity enhancement","Redirection strategy","Time management","User study"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aiki turning online procrastination into microlearning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86144519/Aiki_turning_online_procrastination_into_microlearning.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-384034","identifier":[{"id":"85106686859","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bd5b2ca4-00d7-470d-9d48-128c55c46593"],"keyword":["Aiki","Browser extension","Educational technology","Language learning","Microlearning","Procrastination management","Productivity enhancement","Redirection strategy","Time management","User study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-10D3D295CF59E08C56293FE1D8EAA2A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86144519/Aiki_turning_online_procrastination_into_microlearning.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3411764.3445202","pages":"1-13","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"CHI '21: Proceedings of the 2021 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106686859"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bd5b2ca4-00d7-470d-9d48-128c55c46593"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Aiki - Turning Online Procrastination into Microlearning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384034","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Technical debt is a metaphor which is used to characterize the compromise between short-term benefit and long-term health of a software system. Technical debt is created when software engineers knowingly or unknowingly introduce shortcuts in the development or maintenance of the software system. Therefore, it is crucial to manage the established debt. The aim of this paper is to establish an outline of what we know about Technical Debt Management, the methods applied to gain this knowledge and what we need to know from future studies. This is accomplished through a systematic literature review, which focuses on the concept technical debt management. We identify and analyze 31 papers, which were published from 2017 to April 2019. Our primary analytical focus is on the research approach and setting of the data collection. We identify several gaps in the existing literature: an absence of theory explaining the relation of events, a lack of techniques, such as observation, thus study actual technical debt management behavior, and the unavailability of studies conducted in the public sector. Finally, we offer suggestions for how these gaps can be addressed.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Mille Edith","Østergaard Madsen, Christian","Lungu, Mircea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382290"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Systematic literature review","Technical Debt Management","Technical debt"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systematic literature review technical debt management","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382290","ids":["itu-44d99aec-0b85-441a-a16c-bcbd18e83358"],"keyword":["Systematic literature review","Technical Debt","Technical debt management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BBAABF704CD683851C2F2BBC9ED26F62"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Research Centre for Government IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mille Edith","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Mille Edith","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"østergaardmadsenpau","last":"Østergaard Madsen","locid":"74a08deb-18e1-48d0-a86e-ed6675da92ab","name":"Østergaard Madsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5984-561X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-44d99aec-0b85-441a-a16c-bcbd18e83358"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Systematic literature review: Technical debt management","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382290","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In immersive augmented reality (IAR), users can wear a head-mounted display to see computer-generated images superimposed to their view of the world. IAR was shown to be beneficial across several domains, e.g., automotive, medicine, gaming and engineering, with positive impacts on, e.g., collaboration and communication. We think that IAR bears a great potential for software engineering but, as of yet, this research area has been neglected. In this vision paper, we elicit potentials and obstacles for the use of IAR in software engineering. We identify possible areas that can be supported with IAR technology by relating commonly discussed IAR improvements to typical software engineering tasks. We further demonstrate how innovative use of IAR technology may fundamentally improve typical activities of a software engineer through a comprehensive series of usage scenarios outlining practical application. Finally, we reflect on current limitations of IAR technology based on our scenarios and sketch research activities necessary to make our vision a reality. We consider this paper to be relevant to academia and industry alike in guiding the steps to innovative research and applications for IAR in software engineering.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Merino, Leonel","Lungu, Mircea","Seidl, Christoph"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382130"],"event":{"acronym":"SANER","title":"IEEE International Conference on Software Analysis, Evolution and Reengineering"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Stuttgart"],"keyword":["Software Engineering","Virtual reality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unleashing the potentials of immersive augmented reality for software engineering","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85506912/2001.01223.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382130","identifier":[{"id":"85083593778","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3ae8a471-9418-461a-bfa7-b95c94579cea"],"keyword":["software engineering","virtual reality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-96F346964CB5A6887211286B4D520510"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85506912/2001.01223.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of stuttgart","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Stuttgart","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leonel","key":"merinopau","last":"Merino","name":"Merino, Leonel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph","key":"seidlpau","last":"Seidl","locid":"fda8c630-1b0a-4910-ae2a-602850616275","name":"Seidl, Christoph","orcid":"0000-0003-4539-8297","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/saner48275.2020.9054812","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of The 27th IEEE International Conference on Software Analysis, Evolution and Reengineering (SANER)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083593778"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3ae8a471-9418-461a-bfa7-b95c94579cea"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Unleashing the Potentials of Immersive Augmented Reality for Software Engineering","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382130","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, the evolution of software ecosystems and the detection of technical debt received significant attention by researchers from both industry and academia. While a few studies that analyze various aspects of technical debt evolution already exist, to the best of our knowledge, there is no large‐scale study that focuses on the remediation of technical debt over time in Python projects—that is, one of the most popular programming languages at the moment. In this paper, we analyze the evolution of technical debt in 44 Python open‐source software projects belonging to the Apache Software Foundation. We focus on the type and amount of technical debt that is paid back. The study required the mining of over 60K commits, detailed code analysis on 3.7K system versions, and the analysis of almost 43K fixed issues. The findings show that most of the repayment effort goes into testing, documentation, complexity, and duplication removal. Moreover, more than half of the Python technical debt is short term being repaid in less than 2 months. In particular, the observations that a minority of rules account for the majority of issues fixed and spent effort suggest that addressing those kinds of debt in the future is important for research and practice.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Tan, Jie","Feitosa, Daniel","Avgeriou, Paris","Lungu, Mircea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381916"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Groningen"],"keyword":["Software ecosystems","Software evolution","technical debt repayment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolution of technical debt remediation in python a case study on the apache software ecosystem","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/smr.2319","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381916","identifier":[{"id":"85096653422","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2bd1f716-8647-4514-8b94-1b99d56a31a4"],"keyword":["software ecosystems","software evolution","technical debt repayment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-08187D372F4C23FCAFB0BEA818819DE5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/smr.2319","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85506876/smr.2319.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"university of groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"tanpau","last":"Tan","name":"Tan, Jie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"feitosapau","last":"Feitosa","name":"Feitosa, Daniel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paris","key":"avgerioupau","last":"Avgeriou","name":"Avgeriou, Paris","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/smr.2319","issn":["20477473","20477481"],"issn_org":["1532060X"],"journal":"Journal of Software: Evolution and Process","pages":"1-25","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Journal of Software: Evolution and Process"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096653422"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2bd1f716-8647-4514-8b94-1b99d56a31a4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolution of technical debt remediation in Python: A case study on the Apache Software Ecosystem","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381916","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Technical debt is created when software engineers knowingly or unknowingly introduce shortcuts or unsuitable choices in the development or maintenance of the software system, that will have a negative impact on the future evolution of the system until corrected. Therefore, it is crucial to manage established debt particular in the public sector. The aim of this study is to introduce Technical debt to the field of Digital Government. We create an overview of the state of the art of the knowledge on technical debt management, the methods applied to gain this knowledge, and propose a research agenda to Digital Government scholars. We conduct a systematic literature review, which focuses on the concept of technical debt management. Forty-nine papers published within 2017–2020 are selected and analyzed. We identify several gaps in the existing literature: 1) an absence of theory explaining the relation of events, 2) a shortage of studies conducted in the public sector, 3) and an absence of specific techniques such as observation to study actual technical debt management behavior.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Mille Edith","Østergaard Madsen, Christian","Lungu, Mircea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384568"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Managing legacy systems","Systematic literature review","Technical Debt Management","Technical debt"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"technical debt management a systematic literature review and research agenda for digital government","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85328512/paper_39.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384568","identifier":[{"id":"85085033517","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e07ae5ac-21e5-4930-8513-074615be7a25"],"keyword":["Managing legacy systems ·","Systematic literature review","Technical Debt Management","Technical debt"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0C281378B9957865847BD5634B7AA09A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85328512/paper_39.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Research Centre for Government IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mille Edith","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Mille Edith","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"østergaardmadsenpau","last":"Østergaard Madsen","locid":"74a08deb-18e1-48d0-a86e-ed6675da92ab","name":"Østergaard Madsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5984-561X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-57599-1_10","pages":"121-137","publisher":"Springer","series":"LCNS International Conference on Electronic Government","status":"p","title":"Electronic Government. EGOV 2020. Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"12219"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096502861"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e07ae5ac-21e5-4930-8513-074615be7a25"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Technical Debt Management : A Systematic Literature Review and Research Agenda for Digital Government","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384568","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Learning the vocabulary of a new language and a new programming API are similar in multiple ways. In this paper we evaluate several of the similarities and show that based on them we can design systems that can guide the learner towards improving their knowledge without an external tutor or preset curriculum. Instead, the class of systems we propose here are based on automated approaches of building maps of knowledge of the domain by mining repositories. By intersecting this knowledge with models of learner knowledge built by observing past learner interactions with artifacts of the domain we can generate highly personalized learning guidance.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Lungu, Mircea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381273"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Ecosystems","Education","Software Architecture","Software Engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing personalized learning environments throughmonitoring and guiding user interactions with code andnatural language","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84591910/EASEAI_Designing_Personalized_Learning_Environments_6_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381273","identifier":[{"id":"85077821016","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-017d8916-695f-4215-b559-ad58b15f3695"],"keyword":["Software Architecture","artificial intelligence","ecosystems","education","software engineering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-85D103E46815C4E39BACB8E6BDC1C61B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84591910/EASEAI_Designing_Personalized_Learning_Environments_6_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mircea","key":"lungupau","last":"Lungu","locid":"02960d47-7677-4b2c-99d4-490a31fd6885","name":"Lungu, Mircea","orcid":"0000-0003-3944-5261","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3340435.3342724","isbn":["9781450368520"],"pages":"5-8","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 1st ACM SIGSOFT International Workshop on Education through Advanced Software Engineering and Artificial Intelligence"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077821016"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-017d8916-695f-4215-b559-ad58b15f3695"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing Personalized Learning Environments throughMonitoring and Guiding User Interactions with Code andNatural Language","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381273","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Application Programming Interfaces (APIs) are critical to improve developer productivity: developers can reuse a significant amount of functionality instead of writing it themselves. The flip side of API popularity is that APIs are large and numerous: developers often spend significant time searching for the functionality they need. Worse, they may not even be aware that an API exists for a given task and thus waste time reinventing the wheel. We argue for API fluency: the ability for developers to internalize how an API is used. The more developers have internalized the APIs they need, the more productive they can become. We propose an approach to improve API fluency, relying on spaced repetition of recommended API elements.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Robbes, Romain","Lungu, Mircea","Janes, Andrea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382085"],"event":{"acronym":"ICSE","title":"International Conference on Software Engineering"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Libera Università di Bolzano"],"keyword":["Apis","Mining Software Repositories"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"api fluency","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84473890/API_Fluency.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382085","identifier":[{"id":"85072059291","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-37526f71-153d-47d7-9c5b-81d3c770d929"],"keyword":["APIs","Mining Software Repositories"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E1DE0CC6635019609C3F961CB3B9FFE1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"